# Sample Ooda CLI Fix Invocation

File: ooda/examples/fix.oot

## Fix a .oo file (interactive)

```sh
ooda fix src/main.oo
```

This invokes `ooda/fix/fix.oo::run_ooda_fix` with the file path. The fix command:
1. Runs `oodac check` on the file
2. Classifies the diagnostic (ecap, etc, eparse, eimp, emust)
3. Asks the user (via TTY) for confirmation
4. Applies at most 8 edits
5. Exits 0 on success

## Dry-run

```sh
ooda fix src/main.oo --dry-run
```

Prints the proposed edits without applying them.

## Auto-yes (no prompt)

```sh
ooda fix src/main.oo --yes
```

Skips the interactive prompt. Use with care.
